## Source and historical evidence limits

`SOURCE_AND_COLLISION.md` identifies primary links, exact inspected bodies
versus metadata-only accesses, actual old literals/proofs, and the precise
scope of each transfer. The main historical pins cover 11 originals, not
all keyword matches. P178's whole manuscript and P200's original definition
and invariant-pivot/recurrent proof were read, not replaced by recovery
summaries. Old row/column sorting, RSK/Foata and min-rotation reflections
were screened out before counting the six proposals.

Lewis–Tefft supplies fixed Ducci background, not CNL's selector theorem;
Dahlberg–Wehner supplies the local-complement definition, not D2LC's
scheduler. Elizalde–Winkler's actual Section 5 is the direct LMH owner.
Garver–Patrias Section 2.3 supplies exact classical Knuth relations and
their stated tableau-equivalence theorem. Lubiw and Aldous–Diaconis were
metadata-only accesses; no unavailable full-body theorem was imported.
Source errors, including mistyped arXiv access and failed PDF/browser
requests, are retained. Search nonhits are not novelty evidence.

The optional external brainstorming Codex MCP was not callable; the
declared fallback was author scouting, not a fabricated external result.
The repository skill fixed exact CPU pilots, predeclared bounds,
proof/source subtraction and no routine confirmation; the proof-writer
discipline kept partial results, conjectural obligations and author value
judgments separate. No source lookup uploads a manuscript, and all
specialist contact/external manuscript activity remains HOLD_EXTERNAL.
The OFS/P208 proofs and code were not read or contributed to.

